## Problem
`LaserQuarryBlockEntity.setCustomBounds` (now `QuarryPhaseRunner.onCustomBoundsSet`) rewinds the mining cursor (`miningX/Y/Z`) and clears `finished`, but does not reset `frameBuildIndex` or `phase`. If `setCustomBounds` is ever called after the quarry has begun building its frame or mining, the frame cursor would resume from its previous index — likely producing nonsensical positions against the resized bounds — and `phase` would not return to `CLEARING` to re-clear the new area.

**Currently latent**: the only caller is `LaserQuarryBlock.setPlacedBy`, which runs once at placement when `frameBuildIndex == 0` and `phase == CLEARING`, so the bug doesn't manifest today. But the function name implies a full reset, and any future caller (in-game resize via wrench, marker re-placement, etc.) would hit it.

## Location
`common/src/main/java/com/logistics/automation/laserquarry/entity/QuarryPhaseRunner.java:75-81` (post-refactor)
`common/src/main/java/com/logistics/automation/laserquarry/entity/LaserQuarryBlockEntity.java:1060-1071` (pre-refactor on `mc/26.1`)

```java
public void onCustomBoundsSet() {
    miningX = 0;
    miningY = 0;
    miningZ = 0;
    finished = false;
    // missing: phase = Phase.CLEARING; frameBuildIndex = 0;
}
```

## Suggested fix
Add `phase = Phase.CLEARING;` and `frameBuildIndex = 0;` to `onCustomBoundsSet` so resizing a quarry's bounds always restarts the full clear → frame → mine sequence against the new area. Also reset `currentTarget` and `breakProgress` via the existing `resetBreakProgress()` helper to avoid the next tick continuing to break the previous target.

## History
Surfaced in PR #406 review. Pre-existing on `mc/26.1`, `mc/1.21.11`, and `mc/1.21.1`. Deferred from the refactor PR.

## Problem
When `tickClearing` finishes the clear area and switches phase to `BUILDING_FRAME`, it calls `setChanged()` but not `syncToClients()`. Clients only see the phase change on the next tick that flips the energy sync condition — typically the first frame-build tick when `consumeEnergy()` fires. Until then, the probe display and any phase-driven renderer state remain stale (up to 1 tick of "still clearing" after the server has moved on).

In practice this is minor because the next tick almost always consumes energy and triggers a sync, but it's an inconsistency worth fixing.

## Location
`common/src/main/java/com/logistics/automation/laserquarry/entity/QuarryPhaseRunner.java:109-113` (post-refactor)
`common/src/main/java/com/logistics/automation/laserquarry/entity/LaserQuarryBlockEntity.java:223-229` (pre-refactor on `mc/26.1`)

```java
if (target == null) {
    phase = Phase.BUILDING_FRAME;
    frameBuildIndex = 0;
    be.setChanged();
    return;        // <-- no syncToClients()
}
```

The `tickBuildingFrame` → `MINING` transition *does* call `syncToClients()` — the CLEARING → BUILDING_FRAME transition should match for consistency.

## Suggested fix
Add `be.syncToClients();` after `be.setChanged();` in the phase-transition branch.

